  "goodToKnow": "Der Sarg is a coffin. In Germany, there's a strict Friedhofszwang (burial compulsion): remains generally must be buried in a cemetery, either in a Sarg or as ashes in an Urne; scattering ashes at home is mostly not allowed, though some states have relaxed this. Cremation is now more common than coffin burial. Idiom: ein Nagel zu jemandes Sarg (a nail in someone's coffin). From Greek sarkophagos. Plural: die Särge."
